  "details": "Setting up my facial animation controller I noticed some similarity in the patterns where I was using two completely different VRC behaviours for essentially the same thing.\nCase 1: When animating to eye shapes which are closed, I want to disable blinking, so I take control of the eyes using VRCAnimatorTrackingControl and then release it after\nCase 2: When animating to mouth shapes which are open, I want to reduce visemes, so I take control of the mouth using VRCAnimatorLayerControl and then release it after.\nFor some reason one of these uses \"tracking control\" and one of them uses \"layer control\".\nI think it would simplify things conceptually to consider tracking to be a layer, and then allow blending it the same as layers.",
